& [FieldTypes]
  + UUIDs are nonnil lowercase hyphenated identifiers; digests use existing ContentDigest with sha256 lowercase hex; key and signature hex are lowercase of length 64 and 128 respectively
  + timestamps byte counts sequence expected_sequence and total_artifact_bytes are u64; maximum_attempts automatic_retry_count automatic_cleanup_count artifact_count deterministic_replay_count and required_fresh_process_replay_count are u8
  + numeric effect counters and effect_count are u32; physical_contact and fixture_only and all correspondence or authority fields are bool
  + comparison_outcome is exactly before_snapshot_interval within_snapshot_interval or after_snapshot_interval; input_class is existing KcvInputClass
  + authority_packet_request is existing B1OaprRequest; evidence_references is one through forty-eight unique nonempty bounded opaque strings never resolved
  + artifacts is an ordered fifteen-entry array; each artifact has exact fields path bytes sha256 with direct-child path string u64 bytes and ContentDigest
  + all remaining scalar labels profiles statuses contexts and publication hashes are strings; forms deny unknown fields

& [CanonicalOrderAndDigests]
  + compact serde typed struct declaration order matches each ordered list above; canonical reserialization must equal input exactly so duplicate fields reordered fields alternate escaping whitespace or trailing forms refuse
  + semantic digest substitutes sha256(empty bytes) for its own digest field without changing field shape; other fields remain present
  + signature payload clears signature_hex and substitutes sha256(empty bytes) for witness_sha256 then serializes the complete witness struct
  + witness signature input is UTF-8 cantor-b1-time-witness-signature/0.1 then one zero byte then canonical payload
  + witness request receipt and evidence digest domains are cantor.b1.time-witness.digest.v1 cantor.b1.time-witness.request.v1 cantor.b1.time-witness.receipt.v1 and cantor.b1.time-witness.evidence-manifest.v1 followed by zero byte and normalized canonical form
  + retained file raw hashes include exactly one LF terminator; raw candidate descriptor hashes exclude that transport LF and cover the canonical candidate bytes only

& [IdentityAndExpectations]
  + fixture candidate_label is fixture_a4_time_witness_candidate and external candidate_label is external_a4_time_witness_candidate
  + witness UUID authority_label public key and sequence match separately supplied request expectations; label is nonempty bounded text and cannot confer authority
  + witness public key need not equal policy or revocation responder key; target policy fingerprint remains exact from A3
  + witness binds A3 packet and receipt snapshot semantic digest raw snapshot digest A1 A2 receipts and subject policy identities; it never embeds its own resulting A4 packet digest

& [Comparison]
  + structural witness bounds are issued <= observed <= expires; positive sequence and request equality do not imply freshness
  + comparison reads only observed and replayed A3 this_update and next_update; both A3 interval endpoints are included in within_snapshot_interval
  + integer comparison without subtraction supports zero and u64 maximum without overflow; inverted A3 interval refuses through predecessor replay

& [EvidenceAndExecution]
  + exactly sixteen named files and fifteen manifest payload entries follow TWV-005; directory membership is sorted only for set comparison while manifest path order remains exact
  + file readers bound size before and during reads and check regular nonlink and Windows reparse conditions; no discovery beyond the caller-supplied directory
  + no private keys in production forms; deterministic fixture signing exists only in tests; writer is one ignored test for a fresh caller-owned directory
